id: pm-39cqqx
title: Mandatory exact-head DeepScan and CodeFactor zero-new-issues release gate
description: "Make hosted static analysis a hard, locally executable release criterion. Verify the current Git commit's DeepScan status explicitly reports zero new issues and the CodeFactor check completes successfully with No issues found; fail on missing, pending, stale, skipped, or ambiguous results. Wire the verifier into strict release readiness, document the pushed-head prerequisite, test every state at literal 100% coverage, and require both app contexts in main branch protection."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:ci","area:quality",codefactor,deepscan,release-gate,static-analysis
created_at: "2026-07-24T22:46:08.676Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T23:34:05.432Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-24T23:34:04.575Z"
author: claude-code-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A local exact-head command fails for DeepScan findings, CodeFactor findings, absent checks, pending checks, and analyzer payloads that do not prove zero new issues; it passes only when DeepScan explicitly reports zero new issues and CodeFactor explicitly reports no issues for git HEAD; strict release readiness invokes the command; main branch protection requires both DeepScan and CodeFactor; focused tests, lint, typecheck, full literal 100/100/100/100 coverage, hosted checks, and manual pushed-head verification pass."
parent: pm-92if
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: completed
expected_result: "Release readiness fails closed unless the exact pushed head proves DeepScan zero new issues, CodeFactor no issues, and strict protected-main requirements for both contexts."
actual_result: "Merged implementation adds the non-skippable exact-head verifier, exhaustive tests, documented workflow, and strict main protection requiring DeepScan plus CodeFactor; exact prior pushed head 6bfcda25 passed with DeepScan 0 new and CodeFactor no issues."
